      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express the following as a constant multiple of a single trigonometric ratio.\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(49^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(49^\\circ\\right)\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Put $x=49^\\circ$. Recall $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin x\\cos x &=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[2\\sin x\\cos x\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=49^\\circ$ and double the whole angle: $2x=98^\\circ$. The result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin\\left(98^\\circ\\right) .\n$$",
